On Sat, 10 Jun 2000, Pierre Abbat wrote:

> In lesson 20, Alice and Rick go to a restaurant, and the prices are stated in
> rupnu. What's the exchange rate between the Lojbo rupnu and the American dollar?

"Rupnu" refers to "some currency unit".  When unspecified, it is the local
currency unit:  pounds in the U.K., dollars in Poland :-).  Since
we don't know where the story is happening, we can imagine any currency
unit, or an imaginary one.

